ibution of this specific LCG trajectory at n=10000. Theoretical arguments about mod-6 bias or mixing properties are suggestive but insufficient to determine whether the actual counts fall within two standard deviations. The only responsible epistemic move is to file the simulation, calibrate it with the first ten pairs, and let the harness apply the tolerance to the returned counts.","optional_refs":[],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":[],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.2}],"simulation_proposals":[{"declared_assumptions":["X_0 = 42 is the initial state before any die is drawn.","die_n uses X_n after the recurrence step, for n=1..10000 (so X_1 is the first state used for a die).","Integer arithmetic in Python is exact and unbounded, so the recurrence is computed without overflow.","The rng argument is not used because the sequence is fully deterministic.","No imports are needed because all operations are basic arithmetic."],"discriminating_purpose":"Produce the exact face-count tallies and the first ten (X_n, die_n) calibration pairs so the harness can hand-verify the recurrence and apply the fairness tolerance to the counts. The program returns evidence, not a verdict.","hypothesis":"The exact LCG recurrence X_0=42, X_{n+1}=(1103515245*X_n+12345) mod 2^31, die_n=1+(X_n mod 6) for n=1..10000 produces six face counts that can be determined only by simulation. The simulation returns the first ten (X_n, die_n) pairs for calibration and the six flat counts (count_1..count_6) plus total as the discriminating evidence. The fairness verdict is NOT baked into the program; the harness applies the two-standard-deviation tolerance to the returned counts.","input_aliases":[],"interpretation_conditions":["The simulation must implement the exact recurrence: X_0=42, X_{n+1}=(1103515245*X_n+12345) mod 2^31, die_n=1+(X_n mod 6), for n=1..10000.","The program returns the six face counts as flat single-segment observables (count_1..count_6) plus total, not a nested structure or boolean verdict.","The program returns the first ten (X_n, die_n) pairs as flat observables x_1..x_10 and die_1..die_10 for hand-verification against the specification.","The program is deterministic and uses integer arithmetic only; no imports, no randomness, no network.","Fairness is adjudicated by the harness, not the program: a count is within tolerance if |count_i - 10000/6| <= 2*sqrt(10000*(1/6)*(5/6)).","The calibration trace (x_1..x_10, die_1..die_10) must match hand computation of the recurrence before any tally is trusted as evidence."],"model_source":"def simulate(inputs, rng):\n    x = 42\n    counts = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]\n    cal = []\n    for n in range(1, 10001):\n        x = (1103515245 * x + 12345) % (2**31)\n        die = 1 + (x % 6)\n        counts[die - 1] += 1\n        if n <= 10:\n            cal.append((x, die))\n    out = {\n        'count_1': counts[0],\n        'count_2': counts[1],\n        'count_3': counts[2],\n        'count_4': counts[3],\n        'count_5': counts[4],\n        'count_6': counts[5],\n        'total': sum(counts),\n    }\n    for i in range(10):\n        out['x_%d' % (i + 1)] = cal[i][0]\n        out['die_%d' % (i + 1)] = cal[i][1]\n    return out","parameter_definitions":[],"request_identifier":"lcg_die_fairness_301b61","requested_observables":["count_1","count_2","count_3","count_4","count_5","count_6","total","x_1","die_1","x_2","die_2","x_3","die_3","x_4","die_4","x_5","die_5","x_6","die_6","x_7","die_7","x_8","die_8","x_9","die_9","x_10","die_10"],"requested_seed_set":[1],"rival_predictions":["All six counts fall within two standard deviations of 10000/6 (fair).","At least one count falls outside two standard deviations (unfair).","The calibration trace does not match the hand-computed recurrence (implementation error)."],"simulation_mode":"sandboxed_python_v1"}]}